Subject: fix(workflow-state): accept an unevaluable investigation pin in a history-less tree

WFI-024 (Status: Applied) established the rule for plugins/ reference
pins: in a tree with no git history, a live-vs-pin mismatch is not
evaluable -- the pin-commit fallback that would justify it cannot run --
so it is accepted rather than diagnosed, while every tree WITH history
keeps the full check. The amendment-oscillation tolerance for
specs/<feature>/investigation.md (66a22b5a) resolves the pinned
generation's bytes through the same git machinery, but never received
the same no-history rule. Consequence: the first feature carrying a
post-review amendment cannot pass tests/repository-release-validation
-- its fixture copies the tree WITHOUT .git, the reconciliation cannot
resolve the pinned bytes, and the checker reports "spec reviewer
manifest input hash is stale" on a tree the with-history checker
accepts. Reproduced on feature/epic-194-a6-lite-integration at both the
pre-merge tip (0d52885a) and the merged head; identical red on PR #246
CI step "Test repository release validation parity" (ubuntu). The
epic-195/196 branches carry the same class.

The change mirrors WFI-024 exactly, in both runtime twins: before
attempting resolution, a history-less tree returns accepted. Wherever
history exists, every existing line runs unchanged and a non-growth
change still fails.

Apply from the repository root:

    git apply --check docs/ci-staging/investigation-nogit-tolerance.patch
    git apply docs/ci-staging/investigation-nogit-tolerance.patch

---
--- a/plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/check-workflow-state.sh
+++ b/plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/check-workflow-state.sh
@@ -270,6 +270,14 @@ investigation_amendment_reconciles() {
   case "$manifest_file" in
     "$REPO_ROOT"/*) relative="${manifest_file#"$REPO_ROOT/"}" ;;
     *) return 1 ;;
   esac
+  # WFI-024's no-history rule, extended to this reconciliation: without
+  # git history the pinned generation's bytes are unreconstructable, so
+  # the growth-only property is not evaluable at all -- accepted, not
+  # evaluated, exactly as plugins_hash_matches already treats a live-hash
+  # mismatch in a history-less tree (e.g. the release-validation fixture,
+  # which copies the tree without .git). Wherever history exists, every
+  # line below runs unchanged and a non-growth change still fails.
+  plugins_git_history_available || return 0
   tmp_pinned="$(mktemp)" || return 1
   if resolve_verified_investigation_pin "$contract" "$expected" "$relative" "$tmp_pinned"; then
     investigation_growth_only_change "$tmp_pinned" "$manifest_file"
--- a/plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/check-workflow-state.ps1
+++ b/plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/check-workflow-state.ps1
@@ -260,6 +260,11 @@ function Test-InvestigationAmendmentReconciles([string]$ManifestFile, [string]$E
     $prefix = $RepoRoot.TrimEnd([IO.Path]::DirectorySeparatorChar) + [IO.Path]::DirectorySeparatorChar
     if (-not $ManifestFile.StartsWith($prefix, [StringComparison]::Ordinal)) { return $false }
     $relative = $ManifestFile.Substring($prefix.Length).Replace("\", "/")
+    # WFI-024's no-history rule, extended to this reconciliation: without
+    # git history the pinned generation's bytes are unreconstructable, so
+    # the growth-only property is not evaluable -- accepted, not evaluated,
+    # matching Test-PluginsHashMatches in a history-less tree.
+    if (-not (Test-PluginsGitHistoryAvailable)) { return $true }
     $tempFile = [IO.Path]::GetTempFileName()
     try {
         if (-not (Resolve-VerifiedInvestigationPin $Contract $Expected $relative $tempFile)) { return $false }
